// Title: Mshtml.DLL RunHTMLApplication Suspicious Usage
// Sigma ID: 4782eb5a-a513-4523-a0ac-f3082b26ac5c
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems),  Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Josh Nickels, frack113, Zaw Min Htun (ZETA)
// Date: 2022-08-14 | Modified: 2024-02-23
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth
// Description: Detects execution of commands that leverage the "mshtml.dll" RunHTMLApplication export to run
//   arbitrary code via different protocol handlers (vbscript, javascript, file, http...)
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/n1nj4sec/status/1421190238081277959
//   - https://hyp3rlinx.altervista.org/advisories/MICROSOFT_WINDOWS_DEFENDER_TROJAN.WIN32.POWESSERE.G_MITIGATION_BYPASS_PART2.txt
//   - http://hyp3rlinx.altervista.org/advisories/MICROSOFT_WINDOWS_DEFENDER_DETECTION_BYPASS.txt
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_mshtml_runhtmlapplication.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\..\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains "mshtml") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "#135" or ProcessCommandLine contains "RunHTMLApplication")
